{"id":571,"name":"zoroark","speciesId":571,"dex":571,"form":"normal","generation":5,"types":["dark"],"stats":{"hp":60,"attack":105,"defense":60,"special-attack":120,"special-defense":60,"speed":105},"abilities":[{"name":"illusion","hidden":false}],"height":16,"weight":811,"baseExp":179,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/571.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/571.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/571.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/571.ogg","genus":"Illusion Fox Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon Ilusão Raposa","flavor":[{"version":"black","text":"Bonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents."},{"version":"white","text":"Each has the ability to fool a large group of people simultaneously. They protect their lair with illusory scenery."},{"version":"black-2","text":"Stories say those who tried to catch Zoroark were trapped in an illusion and punished."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"It doesn’t just transform itself—it also has the power to make hundreds of people see its illusions."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"If it thinks humans are going to discover its den, Zoroark shows them visions that make them wander around in the woods."},{"version":"sword","text":"This Pokémon cares deeply about others of its kind, and it will conjure terrifying illusions to keep its den and pack safe."},{"version":"shield","text":"Seeking to ease the burden of their solitude, lonely Trainers tell Zoroark to show illusions to them."},{"version":"legends-arceus","text":"With its disheveled white fur, it looks like an embodiment of death. Heedless of its own safety, Zoroark attacks its nemeses with a bitter energy so intense, it lacerates Zoroark's own body."}],"flavorP